    {
      "id": "u18-3",
      "title": "Terms of endearment & respect",
      "explanation": [
        "**skat**, **liefie**, **bokkie** = darling, sweetheart (for partners and children).",
        "**Oom** and **Tannie** show respect for any older man or woman. Using **jy** with an older stranger can sound rude: use **u**, or Oom / Tannie.",
        "**Boer maak 'n plan** = \"a farmer makes a plan\": the famous South African can-do attitude, meaning *we'll find a way*. **bekommer** = worry."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "af": "Dankie, Tannie!",
          "en": "Thank you, ma'am!"
        },
        {
          "af": "Moenie jou bekommer nie, boer maak 'n plan.",
          "en": "Don't worry, we'll find a way."
        }
      ],
      "vocab": [
        "skat",
        "liefie",
        "bokkie",
        "boer maak 'n plan",
        "bekommer"
      ],
      "exercises": [
        {
          "type": "choice",
          "question": "You're thanking an older woman at a shop. Most respectful:",
          "options": [
            "Dankie, Tannie!",
            "Dankie, bokkie!",
            "Dankie, ou!"
          ],
          "answer": "Dankie, Tannie!"
        },
        {
